text:
Went to see Ildris.  Met a union leader goblin, she was not what I expected!  Really nice.  Malgrin and Ophira argued about that burning man, and what he said.  Ildris is pretty sure that was Bernard.  {d:Anima miser'da...:Poor unfortunate soul...}

Then Ophira complained about Malgrin AGAIN!  Why can't these two GET ALONG??!!? No {d:pactum:contract} seems to work with them!

Talked with Ophira for a long time.  She told me about her grandfather, and about her childhood.   Seems like she had it good... too good though, maybe.  I feel really bad for her.  But also kind of jealous.  She knew her family, but she lost them all.

I think I got through to her about Malgrin, though, eventually. She said she'll try, at least!

.... {d:Quid'inferi?!:What the fuck?!}

Things have been moving so fast, I've barely even written in here! But after getting to Elidir... I had to write something down! So much has happened, it's all really {d:Nimis'omnia.:Too much, all of it.}

I have to start somewhere. This city is big, really big. Coming in through the central river was really awesome. {d:Vah... vastum.:Oh… vast.} And Ezio, he let us right in, seems to have the dockmaster as a friend, or, I guess, a {d:Emptus.:A bought man.}

We did a lot on our first full day here. It was great to see A & P again (should I learn a code from Leofric?). They are staying on the down-low. We picked up some of the things they left off, no big deal. There were some thieves who broke into the old safe hours, we had to go get something back from them. Their leader, Father Kindness, seemed like a nice guy! He said they weren't supposed to go after us... and Leofric said apparently just the right thing to get him on our side. {d:Cal'acutus.:Smartass.} I think he'll help us!

We also ran into a noble, harrassing a poor man and his crazy big creature. I got... too excited, I think, to fight. Malgrin has really gotten me riled up about the nobles. Leofric came to talk to me about it... and I think he is right. I let my adrenaline get the better of me. I didn't have to threaten the stupid kid. {d:Vah! Stultus sum.:Ugh! I'm an idiot.} I'm too used to using my sword to solve problems. I should remember to smile and wink!

Anyway, it's so {d:Infer'de:fucking} cold here! Malgrin's scarf is helping though.

Okay, I wrote enough. We also met Ezio today for a bit, but I'll write about that.. later. Time to sleep! Tomorrow we're going to get costumes!
